<title>CANADA: TABLE-Canada government cash balances rise in week.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Canada government cash balances rise in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances rose in the week that ended July 9, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					Wk to Jy 9  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  28.37   -0.400    +1.122</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     6.16   +4.342    -0.453</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	456.32   -0.431    -6.532</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 122.80   +2.400   -33.200</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.22   -0.092    +1.925</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   May 97     Apr 97     May 96</p>
<p>M1					  71.01	69.62	61.02</p>
<p>M2					 391.85     390.50     391.67</p>
<p>M3					 505.70     502.76     481.50</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			May	   April</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-14.59	-17.30</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     714.38	708.03</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    102.60	105.66</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
